From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucas gelfond <lucasgelfond@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 17:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] demux: gme: open streams of unknown size

A gzipped VGM (.vgz) reaches gme through the inflate stream filter, which
cannot tell the decompressed size, so Open() gave up before identifying it
and the file did not play. Read such a stream whole, as Open() already
does for a zero-sized one.
---
 modules/demux/gme.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/modules/demux/gme.c b/modules/demux/gme.c
index 47169d7..5d61e1e 100644
--- a/modules/demux/gme.c
+++ b/modules/demux/gme.c
@@ -77,8 +77,10 @@ static int Open (vlc_object_t *obj)
     demux_t *demux = (demux_t *)obj;
     uint64_t size;
 
+    /* A stream of unknown size (a gzipped .vgz, through the inflate stream
+     * filter) is read whole below, as a zero-sized one is. */
     if (vlc_stream_GetSize(demux->s, &size))
-        return VLC_EGENERIC;
+        size = 0;
     if (size > LONG_MAX /* too big for GME */)
         return VLC_EGENERIC;
 
